    <a href="/contact/rfq" class="hana-btn hana-btn-on-dark" style="white-space:nowrap;position:relative;z-index:1;">Start a program <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--hana-blue)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a>
  </div></div></div>
<div style="background:#fff;"><div class="cap-section"><div style="margin-bottom:8px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">Frequently asked questions</h2></div>
    <div style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;">
      <details class="sc-faq" open>
      <summary>What does manufacturing traceability record?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Traceability can cover material and lot information down to reel level, together with process routes, manufacturing parameters, inspection results and test data associated with each serialized unit.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>How does traceability help when a manufacturing issue is identified?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Detailed material and production records allow affected lots or units to be identified and contained more quickly, supported by yield, defect and audit information.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Is traceability available for automotive and medical programs?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Yes. Hana’s traceability systems support the manufacturing record requirements associated with automotive IATF 16949 and medical ISO 13485 programs.</div>
    </details>
